    perf(audit): single-pass ledger read (PERF-2). Addresses PERF-2.
    
    PERF-2: _audit_rows() re-read and re-parsed the ENTIRE
    .lore/validate-history.jsonl once per registry class (14 full passes:
    44,254 json.loads at a 3,161-row ledger, 144 ms; 1.06 s at 10x). New
    lore.validate.last_local_validation_batch() scans the ledger ONCE and
    returns {class_id: newest record}; _audit_rows() does dict lookups.
    Semantics unchanged: newest-wins by FILE ORDER, torn/blank/non-dict
    lines skipped, missing ledger -> {} (baseline rows).
    
    Measured at 4,060 live rows (ledger grew since the row's 3,161
    measurement): in-process _audit_rows 7.8 ms mean (was ~96 ms
    ledger-dependent at 3,161 rows; CLI mean 60.8 ms including the ~48 ms
    interpreter-startup floor). Baseline equivalence and the read contract
    are pinned in tests/test_perf2_audit_single_pass.py (8 tests):
    batch==multi-pass newest per class, newest-by-FILE-ORDER (older
    timestamp in the later position wins), torn/blank/non-dict skip,
    missing-ledger -> {}, record pass-through (env_absent_orders intact),
    CLI JSON unchanged vs baseline, CLI <100 ms budget, class ids derived
    from SEED_CLASSES + UNCLASSIFIED_ID (no hardcoded literals).
    
    Count sync: 536 -> 544 (scripts/test-count.txt, README, INSTALL,
    CONTRIBUTING, skills/lore-usage) — count guard PASS.
    Existing LORE-061 audit tests re-seamed from
    last_local_validation -> last_local_validation_batch.
    
